From: Construct <release@constructlinux.org>
Subject: Expect bind_property_full()'s type error where TypeScript 7 reports it

The thermometer's bind_property_full() calls return what ts-for-gir does
not type, which each marks with @ts-expect-error on the line before it.
TypeScript 7 reports the mismatched overload on its first argument instead
of on the call: the directive found no error on its line ("Unused
'@ts-expect-error' directive") and the error went unexpected. The comments
move onto the argument it reports on; no code changes.

diff --git a/src/app/thermometer.ts b/src/app/thermometer.ts
index f39d426..016a749 100644
--- a/src/app/thermometer.ts
+++ b/src/app/thermometer.ts
@@ -287,10 +287,10 @@ export class Thermometer extends Gtk.Widget {
             GObject.BindingFlags.DEFAULT
         );
 
-        // @ts-expect-error ts-for-gir does not `bind_property_full` correctly. In GJS it actually returns a
-        // tuple of [boolean, value] where the boolean is whether the transformation succeeded, and the value
-        // is the transformed value.
         this.bind_property_full(
+            // @ts-expect-error ts-for-gir does not `bind_property_full` correctly. In GJS it actually returns a
+            // tuple of [boolean, value] where the boolean is whether the transformation succeeded, and the value
+            // is the transformed value.
             'range',
             this.lowLabel,
             'label',
@@ -301,8 +301,8 @@ export class Thermometer extends Gtk.Widget {
             null
         );
 
-        // @ts-expect-error Same as the above.
         this.bind_property_full(
+            // @ts-expect-error Same as the above.
             'range',
             this.highLabel,
             'label',
